                <pb facs="1432" n="1274" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1274"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Meyer to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-01-01"><hi rendition="#italic">January 1,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Consul Smith in Moscow reports to-day by telephone that everything is quieting
                    down; barricades being removed; streets regaining normal condition. American
                    consulate has not been disturbed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Meyer.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
